  "problem": "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}+1, & x\\ne -1 \\\\ 0, & x=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $g(x)?$\n\nI. $g(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$\n\nII. ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x)$ exists\n\nIII. ${lim}_{x\\to \\,(-1)}g(x)=g(-1)$\n\nIV. $g(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=-1$",
